questions.explanation:
Step 1: Calculate the lengths of AB, BC, and AC using the distance formula:
AB = √[(4 - 1)² + (6 - 2)²] = √(9 + 16) = √25 = 5;
BC = √[(7 - 4)² + (2 - 6)²] = √(9 + 16) = √25 = 5;
AC = √[(7 - 1)² + (2 - 2)²] = √(36 + 0) = √36 = 6.
Step 2: Compare the side lengths: AB = BC = 5, AC = 6.
Step 3: Conclude that triangle ABC is isosceles with AB and BC as the congruent sides.
